From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 16:54:19 +0200
Subject: media: sun6i-isp: Default the bayer offsets to unity, not one level
 bright

The pipeline loses a level by construction. The luma coefficients sum to
16383 of 16384, so a uniform field comes out one below what went in, and
the bayer offsets are what cancels that. They reach the matrix divided
by 16, which makes 16 the value that cancels it exactly.

The default was 32, which overshoots by a level in the other direction:
black came out at 1 rather than 0, and every level with it. Measured
over a 192 level sweep with everything else at unity, the output is
v - 1 at an offset of 0, v at 16, and v + 1 at 32.

So this is not a matter of removing the offsets -- doing that would
leave the pipeline a level dark rather than neutral -- but of setting
them to the value that makes a pass-through actually pass through.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c | 19 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c
@@ -23,10 +23,21 @@ static const struct sun6i_isp_params_config sun6i_isp_params_config_default = {
 	.modules_used = SUN6I_ISP_MODULE_BAYER,
 
 	.bayer = {
-		.offset_r	= 32,
-		.offset_gr	= 32,
-		.offset_gb	= 32,
-		.offset_b	= 32,
+		/*
+		 * The pipeline loses a level by construction: the luma
+		 * coefficients sum to 16383 of 16384, so a uniform field
+		 * comes out one below what went in. These offsets are what
+		 * cancels that, and they reach the matrix divided by 16, so
+		 * 16 cancels it exactly and 32 overshoots by the same level
+		 * in the other direction.
+		 *
+		 * Measured over a 192 level sweep: at 0 the output is v - 1,
+		 * at 16 it is v, and at 32 it is v + 1.
+		 */
+		.offset_r	= 16,
+		.offset_gr	= 16,
+		.offset_gb	= 16,
+		.offset_b	= 16,
 
 		.gain_r		= 256,
 		.gain_gr	= 256,
